course: dictionary
lesson: 15953
title: Unsupported: not held up, not backed, not helped
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Break the word into parts. «Un-» means not, and «supported» means held up or backed. So unsupported means not held up, not backed by proof, or not helped by others.
explain: «The shelf was left unsupported, and the books crashed to the floor.» Nothing was holding the shelf up, so it fell. The falling books are the clue. Try the meaning in the sentence: «not held up by anything» makes sense, so you have it.
explain: In school subjects, the word warns you about proof. «The scientist's claim was unsupported by any evidence.» means the claim has no proof yet, so we should not believe it yet. Ask: what would fit here? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Unsupported means not held up, not backed by proof, not helped by other people, or not worked with by a device or program.
fact: «Unsupported claims» are statements with no evidence to back them up.
fact: «The tent stood unsupported» means nothing was holding it up.
fact: On a computer, «unsupported file type» means the device or program cannot open that kind of file.
fact: The «un-» at the start means not, so if you know «supported», you can work out «unsupported».
exercise: «The shelf was left unsupported, and the books crashed to the floor.» What does unsupported mean here? | Very heavy and strong | *Not held up by anything | Full of books | Covered in paint
exercise: «The scientist's claim was unsupported, with no evidence at all.» What does unsupported mean here? | Written in pencil | Very loud | *Not backed by facts or proof | Liked by many people
exercise: Your tablet shows «unsupported file type». What does that mean? | *The device or program cannot open this kind of file | The file is very big | The file is a picture | The file is finished and saved
test: «The young inventor worked unsupported, with no help from anyone.» What does unsupported mean? | Built from wood | *Without help from other people | Very tired
test: Which word means a statement has no proof to back it up? | *Unsupported | Bright | Tidy | Loud
exam: Which sentence uses unsupported to mean nothing is holding it up? | «The unsupported children laughed loudly.» | «The unsupported cake was delicious.» | *«The table was unsupported, so it tipped over when I leaned on it.»
